## 14. Technology and Implementation

Build a maintainable, responsive website with a modern frontend.

Preferred approach:

- React with TypeScript.
- A clean, reusable component architecture.
- Tailwind CSS or an equally maintainable styling system, if supported.
- A structured routing system.
- Centralized brand and product configuration.
- A reusable content structure for services, workshops, products, and articles.
- Accessible forms and navigation.
- Production-ready error, loading, and empty states.

Use the framework and deployment capabilities supported by the current Google AI Studio environment. Do not assume that Google AI Studio itself provides hosting, payment processing, email delivery, a database, or a secure digital-download backend.

If a backend is required, separate the frontend from backend functionality and document the required integrations.

Do not put secret API keys, payment credentials, email credentials, or private tokens in client-side code. Use environment variables and secure server-side configuration.

Keep integrations modular so the website can later be connected to a custom domain, a content-management system, a payment gateway, secure file storage, analytics, and a transactional email provider.

Do not introduce unnecessary infrastructure or paid services when a simpler reliable solution is sufficient.

